<title>USA: TVA seen restarting 1,170 MW Tenn. nuke.</title>
<headline>TVA seen restarting 1,170 MW Tenn. nuke.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tennessee Valley Authority (TVA) was taking its 1,170 megawatt Watts Bar nuclear power plant out of shutdown and planned to synchronize it to the electricity grid Friday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>TVA has a &quot;plan to place unit on line late today,&quot; the NRC said in its daily plant status report for Friday.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Spring City, Tenn., tripped off line March 6 due to a broken shaft on the main feed pump.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
